  "construction": "Two-block group-algebra code C(a,b) of arXiv:2610.13880 (Table 11) over the cyclic group C63 (GAP SmallGroup(63,2)): H_X = (L(a) | R(b)), H_Z = (R(b)^T | L(a)^T) with L and R the left and right regular representations, a = 1 + x^2 + x^16 + x^36, b = 1 + x^19 + x^56 in a generator x of order 63, i.e. the generalized bicycle code with A = a(x), B = b(x). The stored matrices use the qubit ordering of the paper's database (record 1518c4016adc09f8, github.com/gideonlsx/bicycle-race @ aed705a, data/codes.jsonl, CC BY 4.0): qubits 0..62 are the left block and 63..125 the right block, group elements numbered as GAP's Elements(SmallGroup(63,2)) with e0 the identity, x = e5, so a = e0 + e2 + e18 + e32, b = e0 + e4 + e39. Rebuilt from the database's group data; CSS commutation, k, check weight and both of the paper's witnesses were re-checked on the rebuilt matrices.",
